ownerDecisions.decision:
Q-C5-LANE (new; I objected to the lane-method choice and put it to the owner): "On the lane, as C3/C7 (Recommended)". The tick-0 first claims of w1, w2 and w3 in C5 ride the attack lane. This is one rule for every class's scheduled first claims, fixed by precedent and not by the probe:
- packet 1's C3 sends its role workers' tick-0 setup ACQUIREs with lane=True and no event tag (_classes.py@25c9ff0e ReplayStale.before_tick);
- rev 3's own C5 text points to C3 for these claims;
- rev 3's C7 puts its scheduled first claims on the lane.
So "only event-tagged operations ride the lane" doesn't match packet 1. Rev 4 states the rule once, in section 5's method list, and applies it to C5 and C7 alike. For w5's operations (Q3-5), apply the written rule "scheduled events plus the victim's operations on its item" and say which clause covers each operation. Disclose in rev 4 that the probe readings were seen before this decision, and that the owner fixed the rule by precedent.
